            <ArticleTitle>Effect of Xylan Sulfates on Coagulation of Human Blood Plasma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>158-161</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10517-017-3947-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sulfated derivatives of xylan (isolated from Bétula pubéscens wood) with average molecular weight ~34 kDa, sulfur content of 11.3-17.5%, a degree of substitution of 0.74-1.64 are anticoagulants of direct type of action. Antithrombin and antifactor Xa activities in three tested xylan samples did not differ and reached 30.8-31.8 and 13.5-14.3 U/mg, respectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
